# Keep stray Node tooling out of the Railway upload so Nixpacks doesn't
# auto-detect a Node provider and inject an npm build phase. This is a
# Python (Flask) service started via `bash start_web.sh` (railway.json).
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules/

# r-connect (2026-06-25): the local tree had grown to 1.2 GB and `railway up`
# was timing out mid-upload. None of the below is built or served at runtime
# (Flask serves only from static/; the git self-heal at main.py:351 is gated
# to REPLIT_ENVIRONMENT and never runs on Railway). Excluding them cuts the
# upload by ~700 MB. Do NOT add routes/, scripts/, static/, or templates/ —
# those ARE imported/served.
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
infrastructure_output/
dchub-frontend/
docs/
backups/
